    "description": "Iranian e-commerce encompasses broad online catalogs, seller marketplaces, specialist retailers, and channels connecting digital discovery with ordering and delivery. Public platform interfaces reveal different commercial models, while reported national transaction values require careful separation from retail sales, platform revenue, and inflation-adjusted growth. [s1][s2][s3][s4]",
    "tags": ["E-commerce", "Online Retail", "Marketplaces", "Digital Payments", "Logistics", "Iran"],
    "status": null,
    "editorial_status": "needs_research",
    "as_of_date": "2026-10-26",
    "created_at": "2026-10-27T18:51:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-27T18:51:53Z",
    "seo": {
      "title": "E-commerce in Iran: Platforms, Purchasing and Data | Iran, Unfolded",
      "description": "Explore Iran’s online retail models, seller marketplaces, specialist stores, and the limits of reported national e-commerce statistics."
    },
    "content": [
      {
        "id": "different-commercial-models",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Several markets behind one label",
        "content": "Iranian e-commerce becomes easier to understand when different kinds of online business are considered separately. Digikala’s public catalog spans electronics, household goods, clothing, and personal-care products. Basalam presents itself as a marketplace connecting buyers directly with sellers, with categories extending from food and handicrafts to furniture. Khanoumi’s catalog gives greater prominence to cosmetics, skin care, hair care, and personal care, while also listing additional categories. These interfaces document differences in merchandising and presentation; they do not independently establish market leadership or sales shares. [s1][s2][s3]\n\nThe distinction matters because a broad catalog, a seller marketplace, and a specialist retailer organize discovery differently. A broad catalog groups many kinds of purchases within one destination. A marketplace makes the seller relationship more visible. A specialist catalog can organize a product field into more detailed subcategories, as Khanoumi does for skin and hair care. These are interpretations of the inspected interfaces, rather than claims about every transaction each company handles. [s1][s2][s3]",
        "source_ids": ["s1", "s2", "s3"]
      },
      {
        "id": "platform-functions",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "The transaction continues beyond product discovery",
        "content": "The inspected sites also show that online commerce involves more than displaying products. Digikala describes delivery choices and product returns. Basalam presents bank-gateway payment, a refund guarantee, direct communication, and support as parts of its proposition; it also provides seller-management and developer links. These published functions connect the storefront to payment, fulfillment, and the continuing buyer–seller relationship. Their presence on a website does not establish consistent service quality or delivery coverage in every location. [s1][s2]\n\nFor an international reader, Basalam’s emphasis on direct contact is particularly useful for understanding the marketplace model. The seller remains part of the shopping experience rather than disappearing behind a single catalog identity. Its wholesale and organizational-purchasing links also indicate that consumer shopping and purchasing for businesses can coexist within a wider platform ecosystem. They do not establish the size of business-to-business trade. [s2]",
        "source_ids": ["s1", "s2"]
      },
      {
        "id": "reading-national-totals",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "What the reported national values measure—and leave unresolved",
        "content": "A Digiato article published in October 2025 attributes successive annual e-commerce transaction values to the acting head of Iran’s E-Commerce Development Center. The observations reproduced below retain the source’s Solar Hijri year labels and nominal toman denomination. They are reported national aggregates, rather than audited revenue figures for the platforms discussed here. [s4]\n\nThe sequence rises in nominal terms. That alone cannot establish an equivalent increase in the quantity of goods and services purchased: price changes also affect monetary totals. No inflation adjustment or foreign-currency conversion has been applied. More fundamentally, the underlying national report’s full methodology could not be inspected because both the official PDF and an identified mirror returned access errors. The annual values are therefore presented as a reported sequence with unresolved comparability questions, rather than as a validated retail-market trend. [s4]\n\nOnly the consecutive observations explicitly given in the inspected retrospective account are included. Earlier years and more recent full-year results have not been filled in from forecasts, mixed secondary accounts, or assumptions about release schedules. A line chart is withheld until the underlying definitions and treatment of payment channels can be checked.",
        "source_ids": ["s4"]
      },
      {
        "id": "reported-annual-values",
        "type": "table",
        "content": {
          "title": "Reported national e-commerce transaction values, Solar Hijri 1400–1403",
          "dataset_id": "reported-national-transaction-value"
        },
        "source_ids": ["s4"]
      },
      {
        "id": "trust-and-records",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Trust depends on information and follow-through",
        "content": "The Electronic Commerce Act text hosted by WIPO provides historical context for the information accompanying online purchases. Its consumer-protection provisions address supplier identity, costs, contract terms, after-sales information, and withdrawal, with qualifications and exclusions elsewhere in the text. This establishes the subjects addressed by that legislation; it does not establish current enforcement or determine the outcome of a particular dispute. [s5]\n\nThe most useful way to explore this field is therefore to connect each commercial model to its operating responsibilities: who presents the offer, who supplies the item, how payment is handled, and how delivery or returns are addressed. The platform pages make some of these functions visible. National totals answer a different question and should not substitute for evidence about individual businesses, regional access, or consumer outcomes. [s1][s2][s4]",
        "source_ids": ["s1", "s2", "s4", "s5"]
      }
    ],
